"},{"headline":"LSU star LB Whit Weeks exits vs. Texas A&M with foot injury","description":"LSU star linebacker Whit Weeks left Saturday night's game against Texas A&M after heading to the locker room on crutches with a boot on his foot.","published":"2026-09-27T04:47:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50039102/lsu-star-lb-whit-weeks-exits-vs-texas-foot-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU linebacker Whit Weeks says he'll return to Tigers in 2026","description":"LSU linebacker Whit Weeks, a first-team All-SEC selection in 2024 who missed much of this past season with an ankle injury, will return to the Tigers in 2026.","published":"2026-01-01T21:07:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47473199/lsu-linebacker-whit-weeks-says-return-tigers-2026","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU LB Whit Weeks (ankle) out against Vanderbilt","description":"LSU linebacker Whit Weeks will not play against Vanderbilt, as the first-team All-SEC player deals with a bone bruise in his ankle.","published":"2025-10-18T15:02:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/46629203/lsu-lb-whit-weeks-ankle-doubtful-vs-vandy-sources-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU LB Whit Weeks ejected after helmet-to-helmet hit on Vernell Brown III","description":"LSU lost All-SEC linebacker Whit Weeks after he was ejected for targeting early in the first quarter on Saturday night against Florida.","published":"2025-09-14T00:46:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/46248593/lsu-lb-whit-weeks-ejected-helmet-helmet-hit-vernell-brown-iii","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4871034/whit-weeks","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whit_Weeks"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Whit Weeks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whit_Weeks","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:28Z","intro":"Whit Weeks (born January 7, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the LSU Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Weeks attended Oconee County High School in Watkinsville, Georgia. As a senior, he racked up 104 tackles, two sacks, and three interceptions on his way to being named Region 8-3A Player of the Year. He committed to Louisiana State University (LSU) to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at LSU in 2023, Weeks played in 11 games with three starts and had 50 tackles and 0.5 sacks.\nWeeks entered his sophomore year in 2024 as a starter. Against the Ole Miss Rebels, he had 18 tackles and one sack. In 13 total games during the season, Weeks recorded 125 combined tackles, 3.5 sacks, 1 interception, 3 pass deflections, and 2 forced fumbles. On January 2, 2025, Weeks underwent surgery to repair a broken fibula that he suffered in the 2024 Texas Bowl."}]}}